course: dictionary
lesson: 9742
title: Sunspots: dark patches on the Sun
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A sunspot is a dark patch on the surface of the Sun. It looks dark because it is cooler than the areas around it. «Sunspots are darker, cooler patches where strong magnetic fields stop hot gas rising.»
explain: Sunspots are not really black. They look black only because the rest of the Sun is much brighter. Some are bigger than the Earth, and scientists count them to study how active the Sun is.
explain: Watch the clues around the word. In a science text, words like Sun, magnetic and gas tell you the meaning. In travel talk, «a holiday sunspot» means a warm, sunny place to relax. The sentence around the word decides which meaning you need.
fact: A sunspot is a dark, cooler patch on the surface of the Sun.
fact: Sunspots look black only because the rest of the Sun is brighter.
fact: The number of sunspots rises and falls in a cycle of about eleven years.
fact: Sunspots move across the face of the Sun, which is how astronomers first noticed that the Sun spins.
fact: Activity from the Sun can cause bright auroras, the northern lights, on Earth.
exercise: «Sunspots are darker, cooler patches on the Sun.» What is a sunspot? | A warm, sunny place where people go on holiday | A star far away in space | *A dark, cooler patch on the surface of the Sun | A hot, bright flame that shoots off the Sun
exercise: «Sunspots look black only because the rest of the Sun is brighter.» Why do sunspots look black? | *Because the rest of the Sun is brighter | Because they are closer to the Earth | Because they are made of coal | Because they are hot and burning
exercise: Scientists count sunspots. Why do they do this? | *To study how active the Sun is | To make the Sun brighter | To find the best sunny holiday resort | To measure the length of a day on Earth
test: «The number of sunspots rises and falls in a cycle of about eleven years.» What is this pattern called? | Magnetic field | Sunspot holiday | Solar wind | *Sunspot cycle
test: Aziz reads in a travel brochure, «a holiday sunspot». What does it mean? | A cold, wet beach | A cloud over the sea | *A warm, sunny place where people go on holiday | A dark patch on the Sun
exam: Which sentence uses sunspot in the science sense? | «The sunspot in the travel guide had cheap hotels.» | «We found a lovely sunspot for our holiday by the sea.» | «The sunspot was full of people at the beach.» | *«Sunspots are dark, cooler patches on the surface of the Sun.»
